{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "D6.2.1/D6.3.2: MVP wide identities use owned homes and native float identities need no boxing. Inlined consumers keep noncollecting length calls and native stack probes; only cold capacity growth can reserve side stacks. D6.2.3: native wide inputs publish boxed values by storing directly into their precise scalar homes.",
